# E20 RemoteMessages: one process per container in the C#, two environments on the loopback transport in the C++; the
# console of each container is compared in its own section. The lines of the C# Container class (connection to the
# server, registration, "Running MAS...") are not compared: the server and the containers are not ported, the
# transport plays their part. A message from another container names its sender "name@container" in the C#, by its
# id in the C++ (the receiver does not know its name, a known divergence of the library): its sender is not compared.
section ^This is Container\d$
ignore ^$
ignore ^Container connecting to server\.\.\.$
ignore ^Container connected to server\.$
ignore ^Container\d registered\.$
ignore ^Running MAS\.\.\.$
cover all
fact setup ^\[(ping-agent|pong-agent)\] (.+)$
fact received ^\t\[\S+ -> (ping-agent|pong-agent)\]: (.+)$
same setup seq by 0
same received seq by 0
check setup count == 2
check received count == 3
